Hi Pablo,

Are you trying to estimate abundance or occurrence probability? The definition of detection probability is context specific. It would also be nice to know how you sampled (number of sites, replicate observations, distance data?, etc..)... but unfortunately, even with this info there is no golden rule. You generally need to do a simulation study to determine the level of precision you might expect for a given sample size.

Richard

