Hello Richard,

Below are my parameter estimates for the exp. negative binomial model that caused the NaN error messages. I've included the backTransformed abundance estimates which don't seem out of the ordinary; however, when I look at my detection probability with GetP(fitted model) they are incomprehensible (p >> 1). I'm not sure how to proceed with this model given the errors and that the parboot fails to run. I've played with K values (to K=200) with no success. Any thoughts would be appreciated.

Thanks, Erik

Call:

gdistsamp(lambdaformula = ~stnd.ag <http://stnd.ag> + stnd.well, phiformula = ~1,

    pformula = ~1, data = umfsp1, keyfun = "halfnorm", output = "density",

    unitsOut = "ha", mixture = "NB")

